$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General/Typical Procedure:
2-Amino-4-bromo-N-(((2S*,5R*)-5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)-methyl)benzamide
(rac-8b). DIPEA (1.15 mL, 6.94 mmol) and HATU (1.32 g, 3.47 mmol) was
added to the suspension of 2-amino-4-bromobenzoic acid (5) (0.5 g, 2.31
mmol) in dry DCM (20 mL), and the mixture was stirred at rt for 15 min.
Then 5-phenyltetrahydrofuran-2-yl)methanamine (rac -7b) (0.36 mL, 3.47
mmol) was added, and the mixture was stirred at rt for 2 h. The solvent
was then removed in vacuum, and the remaining residue was purified by
column chromatography (1/1 = EtOAc/PE),
N-(1-Oxaspiro[4.5]decan-2-ylmethyl)-3-aminobiphenyl-4-carboxamide (9f).
Prepared in analogy to compound rac-8b. Yield 0.10 g (77%), yellowish
oil. 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 1.29-1.79 (m, 14H), 3.41 (dt, J = 13.6
Hz, 5.8 Hz, 1H), 3.65 (ddd, J = 13.6 Hz, 5.6 Hz, 3.6 Hz, 1H), 4.15 (ddd,
J = 16.3 Hz, 9.7 Hz, 5.3 Hz, 1H), 5.61 (brs, 2H), 6.42-6.54 (m, 1H),
6.84-6.96 (m, 2H), 7.30-7.45 (m, 4H), 7.52-7.58 (m, 2H). 13C NMR (75 MHz,
CDCl3): δ 23.7, 24.1, 25.6, 28.6, 36.0, 37.4, 38.6, 43.4, 76.5, 83.4,
114.9, 115.6, 115.7, 127.0, 127.6, 128.8, 128.7, 140.3, 145.0, 149.1,
169.1. HRMS (ESI/TOF-Q) m/z: [M+H]+ calcd for C23H29N2O2, 365.2229;
found, 365.2227.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
