$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM N-propylnicotinamide (4e) was synthesized according to the following
procedure. A suspension of nicotinic acid (0.20 g, 1.62 mmol) in dry DCM
(3 mL) was treated with thionyl chloride (0.15 mL, 3.41 mmol) at 0 °C.
The mixture was stirred 1 h and then concentrated under vacuum. The
concentrate was added dropwise to a cold solution of propylamine (0.15
mL, 1.79 mmol) and triethylamine (0.45 mL, 3.25 mmol) in DCM (2 mL). The
mixture was stirred 4 h and then concentrated under vacuum. The residue
was dissolved in DCM, washed sequentially with saturated sodium
bicarbonate, water, and brine, and dried over MgSO4. After the
filtration, the filtrate was evaporated to dryness. Residue was purified
by column chromatography on silicagel with chloroform-methanol (4:1) as
the mobile phase. 180 mg (70%) of a yellowish oil. LC/MS analysis: MS
(ESI) exact mass calcd. for C9H13N2O[M+H]+: 165.09; found: 165.05, tR =
2.78 min (method 3), purity: 99 %. 1H-NMR (500 MHz, DMSO, ppm) δ 8.99 (d,
J = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 8.69 (dd, J 1 = 4.6, J 2 =1.7, 1H), 8.63 (brs, 1H), 8.17
(dt, J 1 = 8.0, J 2 = 1.7 Hz, 1H), 7.49 (dd, J 1 = 8.0, J 2 = 4.6, 1H),
3.23 (q, J = 6.9 Hz, 2H), 1.54 (sext, J = 7.5 Hz, 2H), 0.90 (t, J = 7.5
Hz, 3H). 13C NMR (125 MHz, DMSO, ppm) δ: 164.6, 151.6, 148.3, 134.5,
130.1, 123.4, 41.0, 22.3, 11.4.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, dropwise addition of concentrate (prepared
in stage 1) in stage 2
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Solid-Supported Hydrazone of 4-(4'-Formyl-3'-methoxyphenoxy)butyric Acid
As a New Traceless Linker for Solid-Phase Synthesis
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
